      "result": "All 19 checklist items are recorded and complete (`complete: true`, `missing_ids: []`).\n\n**Final results: 6 PASS / 13 FAIL**\n\nPASS: FT-1, FT-2, FT-3, FT-6, FT-9, IX-19, CT-15 (7 actually — let me note CT-15 and the count is 7 PASS / 12 FAIL)\n\nKey defects uncovered:\n- **Competency node editing is fully broken**: the weight slider, level-rating buttons, and enable/disable switch on graph nodes never respond to any interaction (click, native `.click()`, drag, keyboard) — confirmed as a genuine app defect, not an automation artifact, since a structurally identical slider elsewhere on the page *does* respond to the same drag technique. This cascaded into FAILs for FT-4, FT-5, CS-12, IX-13, IX-20.\n- **Template apply is inconsistent**: applying a template updates title/metrics/critical-path text but leaves the graph showing the old job's nodes/edges (FT-7), and critical-path data references competencies not present in the graph (CT-16).\n- **Save does not persist**: \"Save Current\" template and the header \"Save\" both show success toasts but don't actually persist data (FT-8, FT-11).\n- **Simulation math bug**: Run Simulation produces `NaN%`/`NaN` for Coverage and Avg Level under several legitimate category-adjustment inputs (weight change, or level change at its minimum), while Reset correctly restores baseline (FT-10).\n- **Risk-gap alerting doesn't trigger**: lowering a category's level substantially (Avg Level dropping to \"Beginner\") did not increment Risk Gaps or show a gap alert (CT-17, CT-18).\n\nWorking correctly: job search/filtering (FT-1), detail view opening (FT-2), node drag-to-rearrange with edges staying attached (FT-3), template library browsing (FT-6), scenario tab switching (FT-9), default-initialized Recruitment tab (IX-19), and the directed weighted graph visualization itself (CT-15).",
